<BaseLayout title="Curation Lab | A name can change, its sources stay attached | David Blumenau" description="Replay a real PanelForge endpoint proof with fictional knowledge triples: two product fields normalized, four source links retained, and an auditable immediate inverse.">
  <main id="main" class="cl-page">
    <section class="cl-hero wrap" id="top"><a href="/labs/" class="cl-back"><Icon name="arrow-left" /> All demonstrations</a><div class="cl-hero-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Curation Lab / Names, sources and a way back</p><h1>A name can change.<br /><em>Its sources stay attached.</em></h1></div><div><p>A small correction can touch more than one relationship. See exactly what changed, where each fact came from, and what an immediate inverse restores.</p><a class="cl-start" href="#cl-title">Follow the recorded edit <Icon name="arrow-down" /></a></div></div><p class="cl-disclosure"><Icon name="check" /> Actual Laravel endpoint execution · fictional data · recorded replay</p></section>
    <div class="wrap"><CurationLab /></div>
    <section class="cl-capture wrap" aria-label="A captured replay state"><details><summary>View a captured merge state <Icon name="image" /></summary><figure><a href="/media/curation/recorded-merge.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/media/curation/recorded-merge.png" width="1328" height="1526" loading="lazy" alt="Curation Lab portfolio replay showing two normalized product fields, four retained sources and two unchanged control rows" /></a><figcaption>A capture of this portfolio replay. It displays synthetic results recorded by the actual Laravel endpoint test; it is not a shipped PanelForge screen. <a href="/media/curation/recorded-merge.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the full-size replay capture <Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a></figcaption></figure></details></section>
    <section class="cl-context wrap"><div><p class="eyebrow">Two different ways to explore memory</p><h2>Understand the sample.<br /><em>Inspect the edit.</em></h2></div><div><p>Memory Lab explains the shape of a reviewed knowledge-graph sample. This Curation Lab follows a separately executed write-and-inverse proof with synthetic fixtures.</p><p>A name is useful for finding things. A retained source is what lets someone inspect why a relationship exists.</p><a class="text-link" href="/labs/memory/">Explore the Memory Lab illustration <Icon name="arrow-right" /></a><br /><a class="text-link" href="/work/knowledge-graph/">Read the knowledge-graph story <Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a></div></section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
